{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Is this a practice quiz for students, a check after training, or a warm-up for a team workshop?","Which topics has your group actually covered? Drop any scenario that tests something you have not taught yet.","Should a wrong pick in the open-question round cost a point, or just earn nothing?","Do you need names to track progress, or should it be anonymous so people answer without pressure?"],"howToUseResponses":"Sort by score to see who is ready and who needs support. Then look question by question: the one most people get wrong is where your next lesson should start. The unscored question at the end tells you which topic felt hardest in the learners' own view, which does not always match where they lost points.","customizeSteps":["Rewrite the scenarios around your own product or case study, keeping one point on each correct option.","Move the score bands if you change the number of questions so the top result stays hard to reach.","Share the link with your class or team, or embed it in your course page, and export the results to CSV."],"faqs":[{"q":"What topics should a marketing research quiz cover?","a":"Types of data, sampling, question wording, experiments and reading results. Scenario questions test whether someone can apply these, not just define them."},{"q":"What is the difference between primary and secondary research?","a":"Primary research is data you collect yourself, such as a survey or interviews. Secondary research uses data someone else already collected, such as a census or industry report."},{"q":"Can I use this quiz for a class?","a":"Yes. Share one link, ask for names if you want to track progress, and review the most-missed scenarios in the next session."},{"q":"How is the marketing research quiz scored?","a":"Each correct answer is worth a point. In the open-question round each right pick adds a point and each wrong one takes a point away. The total picks one of three results."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"Marketing research quiz","description":"Ten scored scenario questions on sampling, question wording and reading results.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_marketin00","ref":"welcome","title":"Let's see how you'd run a real research project. Ten scenarios on sampling, questions and results. Take your time with each one.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_marketin01","ref":"name","title":"What's your name?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":60},{"id":"blk_marketin02","ref":"secondary","title":"You read a government census report to size your market. What kind of data is that?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_primary_data","label":"Primary data","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_secondary_data","label":"Secondary data","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_qualitative_data","label":"Qualitative data","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_panel_data","label":"Panel data","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin03","ref":"why_churn","title":"You don't yet know why customers are leaving. What's the best first step?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_a_large_multiple","label":"A large multiple-choice survey","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_in_depth_interviews","label":"In-depth interviews with people who left","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_an_a_b","label":"An A/B test on the pricing page","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_counting_website_visits","label":"Counting website visits","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin04","ref":"bad_question","title":"What's wrong with asking 'How happy are you with our fast and friendly service?'","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_nothing_it_s","label":"Nothing, it's clear","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_it_s_too","label":"It's too short","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_it_asks_about","label":"It asks about two things and suggests the answer","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_it_should_be","label":"It should be a yes/no question","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin05","ref":"random_sample","title":"Every customer on your list has an equal chance of being picked. What is that called?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_a_convenience_sample","label":"A convenience sample","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_quota_sample","label":"A quota sample","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_simple_random","label":"A simple random sample","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_a_snowball_sample","label":"A snowball sample","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin06","ref":"selection_bias","title":"You survey only people who visited your shop last Saturday about your brand as a whole. What's the main risk?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_the_sample_may","label":"The sample may not represent all your customers","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_the_questions_will","label":"The questions will be too long","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_the_data_will","label":"The data will be secondary","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_there_is_no","label":"There is no risk if the sample is large","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin07","ref":"open_questions","title":"Which of these are open-ended questions? Pick all that apply.","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"multi_select","options":[{"id":"opt_what_made_you","label":"What made you choose us over other options?","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_did_you_buy","label":"Did you buy from us in the last month?","image_key":null,"score":-1},{"id":"opt_what_would_you","label":"What would you change about the checkout?","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_rate_us_from","label":"Rate us from 1 to 5","image_key":null,"score":-1},{"id":"opt_tell_us_about","label":"Tell us about the last time you used the app","image_key":null,"score":1}],"minSelections":1,"maxSelections":5,"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin08","ref":"ab_test","title":"Half your visitors see a green button and half see a blue one. What can this test show?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_why_people_prefer","label":"Why people prefer one colour","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_whether_the_colour","label":"Whether the colour change causes a difference in clicks","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_which_colour_your","label":"Which colour your whole market likes","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_nothing_without_a","label":"Nothing without a focus group","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin09","ref":"correlation","title":"Customers who read your newsletter spend more. What can you safely conclude?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_the_newsletter_makes","label":"The newsletter makes people spend more","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_reading_and_spending","label":"Reading and spending are linked, but the cause is unclear","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_high_spenders_never","label":"High spenders never unsubscribe","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_you_should_stop","label":"You should stop other marketing","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin10","ref":"focus_group","title":"What's a common weakness of focus groups?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_one_loud_voice","label":"One loud voice can sway the rest","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_they_only_produce","label":"They only produce numbers","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_they_always_need","label":"They always need thousands of people","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_they_can_t","label":"They can't be recorded","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin11","ref":"nps","title":"A Net Promoter Score question asks customers about what?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_how_much_they","label":"How much they paid","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_how_likely_they","label":"How likely they are to recommend you","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_how_often_they","label":"How often they buy","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_how_they_found","label":"How they found you","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_marketin12","ref":"hardest","title":"No points here: which topic felt hardest?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"dropdown","options":[{"id":"opt_types_of_data","label":"Types of data","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_sampling","label":"Sampling","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_writing_good_questions","label":"Writing good questions","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_experiments_and_a","label":"Experiments and A/B tests","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_reading_results","label":"Reading results","image_key":null}]}],"endings":[{"id":"end_marketin01","ref":"end_thanks","title":"Worth another pass","bodyMd":"Research methods take practice. Review how to write neutral questions and pick a fair sample, then try again.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]},{"id":"end_marketin02","ref":"end_ready","title":"Ready to run the study 📊","bodyMd":"You spotted the biased question, the sampli